<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Siltek H1 earnings rise 18 pct pre-excepts.</title>
<headline>Siltek H1 earnings rise 18 pct pre-excepts.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-exceps (cts) 71.13	vs 60.24</p>
<p>    Shr,post-exceps (cts) 75.12	vs 71.94</p>
<p>    Div, proposed (cts)   19	   vs 16</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   40.15	vs 38.56</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains     2.13	 vs 6.23</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   56.42	vs 57.23</p>
<p>    Tax			 15.59	vs 15.75</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.69	 vs 4.68</p>
<p>    Turnover		  925.93     vs 908.38</p>
<p>Div payable n/a</p>
<p>on register n/a</p>
<p>Full name: Siltek Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Computer concern Siltek said the dividend would be declared before the end of April 1997. The company said it was cautiously optimistic about prospects for the second half.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
